{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>It and its offspring</b> applies to the female, so that it is forbidden to slaughter the mother and the son or the mother and the daughter, and it does not apply to males, and it is permissible to slaughter the father and the son — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 22:28). The Rav rules that the halakhah follows the one who says that we do not take the father's seed into account (Ḥullin 79a), and so is the view of Onkelos (Onkelos on Leviticus 22:28), and this is the correct reading in the Gemara regarding the law of אֹתוֹ וְאֶת בְּנוֹ. But the way of Scripture, when it mentions the female specifically, is to call it פָּרָה, and if so it would have been fitting for Scripture to say, וּפָרָה אוֹ כִּשְׂבָּה אוֹתָהּ וְאֶת בְּנָהּ. Rather, because it mentioned שׁוֹר אוֹ כֶשֶׂב אוֹ עֵז כִּי יִוָּלֵד, and it mentioned the mother and the son וְהָיָה שִׁבְעַת יָמִים תַּחַת אִמּוֹ, it stated that in these mentioned species, which are ox and sheep, there is yet another commandment concerning them, for אֹתוֹ וְאֶת בְּנוֹ — the males mentioned — shall not be slaughtered on one day."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:58:10.330127934Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}